# s3-27: Computer Use harness re-pointed at the core (applied by the wave's DESKTOP-WIRE task, which deletes this file)

## 1. apps/desktop/src/main/computer/harness/core-transport.ts, in the same change as s3-26.wire item 1

`openComputerCore` calls `createDesktopHost` with the options as they are today (`computer: () => null`, `computerAppInput`,
`computerPermissions`, `computerCommand: () => null`). When s3-26.wire item 1 replaces those four options by
`computer: ComputerHostWiring`, change that call to

    computer: {
      mirror,
      permissions: { read: <the same read>, request: () => undefined },
      environment: { ready: app.whenReady(), sources: () => ({ power: powerMonitor, screen }) },
      desktopHostScreen: () => null,
      desktopHostCommand: () => null,
    },

(`powerMonitor` and `screen` from 'electron', through the same dynamic import) and delete the `computerAppInput` option (the mirror
draws the arrow). The same change is owed by apps/desktop/src/main/browser/test-support/core-harness.ts (not this task's file).

## 2. Run-time facts the lead needs

- The core binary is a test-hooks build named by MIXDOGD_TEST_BIN (else MIXDOGD_BIN), started with MIXDOGD_TEST_HOOKS=1 (the env
  dev_computer.rs reads). The doc comment of DevComputerRunParams in v2/computer_host.rs (and its generated copies in
  packages/protocol/src/index.ts) says MIXDOG_DEV_COMPUTER_RUN=1: that name is not read anywhere; fix the comment text when the
  protocol files are next regenerated.
- scenarios-input.ts and scenarios-recovery.ts (s3-28) read ctx.host / ctx.bridge / readDiscovery, which ScenarioContext no longer has:
  ctx.core (call, helperPid(session), mirror) replaces them. tsc of apps/desktop passes except for those two files until s3-28 lands.
